│ results. STUDY DESIGN Retrospective chart review of the computerized medical record. RESULTS Between January 1, 1994 │
│ and June 30, 1995, 24,823 patients were tested for gonorrhea, of whom 19.3% (4791) had positive cultures. Of         │
│ patients with positive gonorrhea cultures, 564 (11.8%) had positive screening cultures and did not receive therapy   │
│ at the time of evaluation. Similarly, screening chlamydial cultures were positive in 1539 (10.9%) of 14,162 patients │
│ screened for chlamydial infection. Forty-four percent (677) of these did not receive presumptive treatment for       │
